nodecode-injection-guard is a rewrite of moneya's moneya/hermes-injection-guard:

  https://github.com/moneya/hermes-injection-guard
  commit 33a44c7331cde46f34aae0b3d44a6d5fd0f0feb3
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 McDonald Aladi (plugin.yaml, as the repository carries no LICENSE file)

Rewritten: the plugin's whole decision path, in Common Lisp. The eight weighted
signal families and their cl-ppcre patterns, the threshold and its scoring
(including the caps on hidden Unicode and encoded blobs), the EXEMPT-families
rule for local file reads, the span redaction, the neutralisation of hidden
characters, instruction-carrying HTML comments, hidden CSS text and oversized
base64 blobs, the untrusted-data envelope with its SECURITY NOTICE and the
defusing of markers inside the payload, the prefix-matched protected tool list,
the enforce/report/off modes, and the rule that a failure answers the original
text untouched. The report of what was blocked (counts by tool and by signal,
the newest entries, never the payload) keeps its shape as the
injection_guard_stats tool and the /injection-guard command.

Left out, and why: the plugin's JSONL audit file on disk and its
INJECTION_GUARD_MODE environment override, because the session ring of the last
50 blocks and the section's mode answer the same questions without writing
files; the Hermes tool_execution middleware itself, which is one :TOOL hook
here, Nodecode having exactly that point; and the plugin's own copy of the
Hermes runtime, its test harness and its demo. Added: injection_guard_scan, a
verb for the paste path the plugin's README names as "the obvious next step",
and a /injection-guard command that takes text as well as reporting.
